  "note": "CANDIDATES, not confirmed resources - every name here was read from Kaseya's official REST docs; none were written from memory. Derivation: the overview page links 209 per-entity pages; for each page the name was taken from the page's own fields (doc filename, overview link text, 'Entity Path: /atservicesrest/v1.0/<X>', and the 'URLs' section). Those four disagree on 13 entities (singular vs plural, e.g. ExpenseItemAttachment vs ExpenseItemAttachments, ResourceTimeOffBalance vs ResourceTimeOffBalances, ConfigurationItemAttachment vs ConfigurationItemAttachments, DocumentArticleAssociations vs DocumentToArticleAssociations), so BOTH doc-sourced spellings are included and the live probe should settle which one resolves. Expect ~13 of the 404s to be the losing half of those pairs, not real gaps. One lowercase artifact ('paymentTerms') was dropped in favour of 'PaymentTerms'. 4 of the 209 pages are TEMPLATES, not entities - '<EntityName>Webhooks', '<EntityName>WebhookFields', '<EntityName>WebhookUdfFields', '<EntityName>WebhookExcludedResources' - so they are excluded from 'entities' and expanded separately under 'derivedWebhookCandidates'. COVERAGE IS PROBABLY PARTIAL: Kaseya's own docs say to use Swagger UI ([zone]/swagger/ui/index, which needs API credentials) to browse the complete entity list, which implies the help-site index may lag the live API. This list is therefore a lower bound on what the API exposes.",
